// A function with an optional parameter cannot be a callback, and it falls
// out of the arity rule rather than needing one of its own. It SHOULD be
// refused (§4.2): an optional parameter is named at the call site, and a
// dispatch site has no name to give, so accepting it would make `by`
// positional here and named everywhere else.
interface Scale { int go(int v); }
int scale(int v, int by = 2) { return v * by; }
Scale s = scale;
print(s.go(3));
